[Music]  lifetime achievement award sponsored by  Cavanaugh Holmes bill moody for nearly  40 years bill has been involved in  promoting managing and coaching squash  and making the sport accessible to the  Newton Abbot community his greatest  achievement is his unwavering dedication  to junior squash 2016 saw bill's 30th  anniversary of being involved in the NA  STC junior section he first became  involved in 1986 running the Saturday  jr. mornings and has been turning up  ever since at the age of 83 bill could  still be seen taking on the juniors at  doubles showing off some of his skills  only in the last year has he actually  hung up his racket Phil started managing  one of the senior teams before starting  club nights to promote squash for all  abilities in an informal and social  environment club nights continued to be  a regular weekly feature at the club and  Bill still turns up to help run the show  Janice and Mike Hindle Jamison Mike  Hindle met as teenagers when they were  both members of Epson and Yul Harriers  they moved to Devon in 1975 and in 1991  after their son showed an interest in  athletics they joined Newton Abbot  Athletic Club where by 93 94 they both  become involved with coaching  officiating team management and  administration they also joined the  committee which they're still part of  today with Mike appointed as club  president and Janice in the role of  membership secretary their love and  passion for athletics is clear for all  to see and the time they've given up for  the people of Newton Abbot is  considerable there is a wide spectrum of  abilities at the club and they make  everyone feel welcome pam terrell 39  years ago pam set up the club which is  known today as king Stainton swimming  club and she soon had a lot of interest  from eager youngsters all wanting to  learn how to swim over the years pam has  devoted all of her spare time to  teaching youngsters to swim she also  feels inclusion is the key to all  ensuring that the club is accessible to  those with more complex needs in a world  that continues to place pressures on the  young people of today Pam provides many  youngsters with a real sense of  belonging encouraging the older members  of the club to teach others she's  inspired so many people over the many  years and she open  in you to inspire many more for years to  come  [Music]  you

